  "Question": "For a parabolic arch bridge, a coordinate system is established with the crown of the arch as the origin. The parabola containing the arch is \\(y=-x^2/8\\) (unit: m). When the water surface is 8 m below the crown, how wide is the water surface in m?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "16",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Set \\(y=-8\\). Then \\(-x^2/8=-8\\), \\(x^2=64\\), and \\(x=\\pm8\\). The water surface has a width of \\(8-(-8)=16\\) m.",
